---\nfor d, H in products(datasets, horizons):\n    for W in cand_W[d]:\n        for seed in seeds:\n            model = CycleNet(head='linear', cycle_len=W, lookback=96, seed=seed)\n            train(model, early_stop_on=val_mse)\n            mse[d,H,W,seed] = evaluate_once(test)\n\n# ---- Stage 3: analysis ----\nW_star[d,H]   = argmin_W mean_seed(mse[d,H,W])            # empirical optimum\nregret[d,H]   = (mse@W_acf - mse@W_star) / mse@W_star\nagree_exact   = frac(W_acf == W_star); agree_near = frac(|\u0394MSE| <= 1%)\nreport tables by ambiguity label; paired significance over seeds;\nsensitivity: capacity-matched rerun on top-2 W per dataset.\n```\n\n## 7. Limitations (documented, not hidden)\n\n- ACF alone is insufficient by design \u2014 harmonics and mixed seasonality inflate multiple lags; hence the mandatory FFT cross-check and the explicit ambiguity rules + fallback (Section 2.E).\n- CycleNet may be insensitive to W within a range (RCF can partially absorb phase shifts), so exact-agreement may understate the method's practical adequacy \u2014 hence the \"near-agreement within 1% MSE\" metric.\n- Agreement on ETT-family/electricity (strong daily seasonality) may not transfer to weakly seasonal series; exchange-rate-style data is named as the expected failure mode but is out of scope unless you supply it.\n- Everything above about CycleNet's internals references the published RCF description; **no CycleNet code exists in /workspace to verify implementation details** (repo contains only task.json), and no run has been executed \u2014 runtime figures are engineering estimates, not measurements.\n\n---\n\n**Awaited from you:** nothing blocking; the design is complete as approved. If you later authorize execution, the open items are data supply and confirming the runtime budget (tight-budget pruning in Section 5 is the default).", "evidence": "Repository observations grounding the design: /workspace contains only task.json (412 bytes) stating the question and \"D